      "notes": "Book recipe is Pan-Roasted Sea Bass with Wild Mushrooms (p.256), made with cod, its named substitute. Fish roasts right on the sauteed mushrooms (475°, 10-12 min to 140°) and the porcini liquid becomes the sauce. One ovensafe 12-inch skillet. Cod flakes more readily than bass — check at the low end (10 min) for 140°F and move it gently. Simplified for shopping: all baby bella mushrooms (no portobello/porcini); use 1/2 cup chicken broth where the book uses the porcini liquid. Brown the mushrooms well — that’s where the flavor comes from now."
